As a supplier of customers, 21Vianet will actively cooperate to complete all required supplier onboarding processes. Common requirements for vendor setup include providing the business license and qualification documents of 21Vianet, filling out the supplier questionnaire, and signing the confidentiality agreement. The details are as follows: 
&nbsp;
**21Vianet Business license and Enterprise Qualifications, Supplier Questionnaire, Signing of Non-Disclosure Agreement（NDA）**
If the customer requests 21Vianet NDA, licenses, and supplier research questionnaires, Microsoft sales can send the following information to Sales Support <salessupport@oe.21vianet.com>：
*   The **FULL NAME** of the customer company in **both Chinese and English**
*   OPP ID
*   What kind of products does the customer intend to purchase?
&nbsp;

Upon receiving the above information, the Sales Support team will jointly coordinate with 21Vianet legal, finance and HR departments to provide the corresponding services.

&nbsp;

During the order review stage after the contract files are generated by Microsoft CE, the orders will be initiated by Microsoft. After being reviewed by 21Vianet, the order will be submitted to Microsoft to transact in the system. Once Microsoft process is completed, the order comes into effect. The ordering process then flows to 21Vianet for the issuance of invoices and other financial steps. 

Order to Cash process completed. 

**Relevant Members &amp; Tools**

*   Relevant parties: Partners, Microsoft CE, Microsoft AE, 21Vianet Sales Support team, Legal team, Finance team.
*   Relevant system: Hermes, MSX Proposal
  
&nbsp;

### Deal Validation Process

**1) OE Review**

During the initial review stage of the contract, Sales Support will collaborate with multiple teams such as 21Vianet's finance and legal teams to conduct the review. Once the review is completed, the contract will be released to partners. For orders that choose E-Sign, Sales Support team will simultaneously submit the reviewed contract to the E-Sign system.

&nbsp;

**2） Waiting For Customer Chop**

*   Customer and/or Partner:
    *   Stamp (Sign)；
*   Partner:    
    *   Scan the stamped contract;
    *   Mail the physical contract to 21Vianet and filling the express number to Hermes (for E-Sign, the stamped contract returns in 21Vianet E-Sign System);
    *   Upload the softcopy of the stamped contract to Hermes as an attachment;
    *   Fill and verify the customer's Org ID;
    *   Submit the Hermes process to OE Processing
    
&nbsp;  
    

**3） OE Processing**

At this stage, 21Vianet will submit the stamped contracts by the customers and partners for internal stamping process. After the stamping process is completed, the contract will flow to the secondary review process. At the same time, the status of customer’s uncommitted overage and overdue debt under their “21Vianet Online Services Premium Agreement (OSPA)” (if any) will be checked. Once it is confirmed that there are no unresolved overage and overdue debt, the order will be submitted to the next stage "Upload Quote".

**Important Note：** If a deal needs to be prioritized, please contact Microsoft AE to inform Microsoft GK team: apbocn@microsoft.com

